@startuml
actor User
participant "AddTaskButton" as Form
participant "TasksProvider" as Frontend
boundary "Spring MVC\nTaskController" as HTTP
participant "TaskServiceImpl" as Service
participant "Repository adapters\n+ Spring Data JPA" as Repositories
database PostgreSQL as DB

User -> Form: Open New task and enter values
Form -> Form: Trim and validate title
Form -> Frontend: createTask(NewTask)
Frontend -> Frontend: Check view, loading, error and title
Frontend -> HTTP: POST /api/tasks\nJSON with boardId = 1, statusId = null
HTTP -> HTTP: Deserialize CreateTaskRequest
HTTP -> Service: createTask(title, boardId,\ndescription, statusId)
activate Service
Service -> Repositories: BoardRepository.findById(1)
Repositories -> DB: Read board and its statuses
DB --> Repositories: Board data
Repositories --> Service: Board
Service -> Service: new Task(null, 1, title,\ndescription, null, null)
Service -> Repositories: TaskRepository.save(task)
Repositories -> DB: INSERT task\nidentity ID, database timestamp
DB --> Repositories: Generated ID
Repositories --> Service: Task mapped from saved TaskJPA
Service -> DB: Transaction commit
Service --> HTTP: Task
deactivate Service
HTTP -> HTTP: TaskResponse.fromDomain(task)
HTTP --> Frontend: 201 Created + TaskResponse
note right of Frontend
POST response body is not read.
end note
Frontend -> Frontend: Increment reloadCount
Frontend --> Form: Promise<void> resolves
Form -> Form: Close modal and clear inputs
Frontend -> HTTP: GET /api/views/{selectedViewId}/tasks
HTTP -> Service: getTasksOfBoardView(viewId)
Service -> Repositories: Load view, tasks and statuses
Repositories -> DB: Read ordered task data
DB --> Repositories: Rows including created_at
Repositories --> Service: Domain values
Service --> HTTP: TaskViewResult
HTTP --> Frontend: 200 + TaskViewResponse
Frontend -> Frontend: setResult(requestKey, data)
Frontend --> User: BoardLayout -> TaskList -> Task
@enduml